    "globalConstraints": "- A run whose record holds no receipt row dispatches every judge with the brief this engine's base produces: no captured prompt of any role contains the token `FACTS:`, and the schedule \u2014 waves, edges, fold epochs, dispatch order, the one review round \u2014 is what it is at BASE.\n- No worker writes an event: every receipt row is appended by the driver \u2014 `appendEvent` in `fleet/run-engine.mjs` or `eventLog.onEvent` in `fleet/publish-fold.mjs` \u2014 and no role file asks a worker to post, edit or read one.\n- A receipt states what was observed and never what to do: `evidence.read` and `evidence.against` are readings, and no rendered `FACTS:` line carries an instruction to a judge beyond the block's own header sentence.\n- A receipt is scoped to the run that wrote it: the matcher reads only rows this run's own process appended \u2014 the engine's in-memory receipts, or the publish fold's own `<runDir>/events.jsonl` \u2014 and never a tag, a hub issue or another run's directory; a relaunch renders nothing of the run before it.\n- The `FACTS:` block is bounded: at most 20 rows, each row's `read` and `against` at most 500 characters, so a block is under 24 KB however many failures the run recorded.\n- Every event kind and every event field this plan writes is already named in `fleet/CONTRACT.md`'s `Receipts (2026-09-16):` paragraph, which wins over `fleet/RUNBOOK.md` on any literal; a task that finds the paragraph wrong on a literal it implements declares the amendment rather than editing the contract silently.\n- A guarded exam file is self-contained at its guarded path: it imports the engine and the sim helpers by their `fleet/tests/`-relative paths and never imports anything under `fleet/tests/exams/`.",
